#
# Relabels /data/cache.
#
# On this device /cache is a symlink to /data/cache. AOSP already has the right
# labels -- system/sepolicy/private/file_contexts:794 maps /data/cache and
# /data/cache/recovery -- but they apply to files created from then on:
# whatever existed before stays "unlabeled". In enforcing mode it shows up at
# once, because system_server can no longer write to /cache/recovery, the
# directory the recovery commands go through, that is, the update path:
#
#   avc: denied { write } for comm="Thread-16" name="recovery" dev="mmcblk0p39"
#     scontext=u:r:system_server:s0 tcontext=u:object_r:unlabeled:s0
#
# From here on the older files get them too.
on post-fs-data
    restorecon_recursive /data/cache
